<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 Feb 2007</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 24.65 bln esc    COUPON: 6.625 pct</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 6.350836</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 6.36  LOWEST: 6.30</p>
<p>BIDS: 52.71 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY: annual</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 12 August 1997</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 158.06 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
